1
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:20,359
Go ahead.

2
00:00:21,559 --> 00:00:22,160
You do it.

3
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:34,219
I forgot.

4
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:36,259
You're just a worker.

5
00:00:36,479 --> 00:00:37,039
Can't bring yourself to do it.

6
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:38,399
Fine.

7
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,140
You two,

8
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:41,039
keep going.

9
00:00:41,479 --> 00:00:41,880
Brother!

10
00:00:42,359 --> 00:00:44,000
Brother, please spare Brother Li!

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,679
I'm begging you!

12
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:47,439
Hurry up!

13
00:00:47,619 --> 00:00:49,060
Or all three of you are stripping today!

14
00:00:50,179 --> 00:00:50,560
Move it!

15
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:54,119
Brother...

16
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:55,420
Forgive me.

17
00:01:03,159 --> 00:01:03,600
Brother Li.

18
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:05,400
Hold your breath, brother.

19
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,700
If you've got the guts, just kill me!

20
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,099
Brother!

21
00:01:18,879 --> 00:01:20,480
Brother Li!

22
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,719
Just spare us, please!

23
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:26,920
Brother Li!

24
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:28,840
Ziwen,

25
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,019
scaring him is enough.

26
00:01:30,299 --> 00:01:31,120
Don't kill him.

27
00:01:40,939 --> 00:01:41,379
Stop.

28
00:01:46,659 --> 00:01:47,079
Brother Li.

29
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,079
Brother Li!

30
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:48,739
A long time ago,

31
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:51,159
I told my brother

32
00:01:51,879 --> 00:01:53,480
I'd never let him be wronged.

33
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,040
Every bit of pain and blood he suffered,

34
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,439
you will

35
00:01:58,459 --> 00:01:59,780
repay tenfold.

36
00:02:07,019 --> 00:02:07,519
Ziwen.

37
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:15,879
Zhuzi.

38
00:02:15,879 --> 00:02:16,500
I'm fine.

39
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:21,080
Brother Tian.

40
00:02:36,439 --> 00:02:36,939
Ziwen!

41
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,060
Ziwen!

42
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,080
Enough, Ziwen!

43
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,699
He wanted me dead, and you protect him?!

44
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:41,860
Ziwen!

45
00:02:41,939 --> 00:02:43,539
If someone dies, there's no turning back!

46
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:44,060
Ziwen!

47
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:44,759
Bro...

48
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:57,120
Drop the knife and save him!

49
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,599
Put the knife down!

50
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,039
Brother Li!

51
00:03:11,879 --> 00:03:12,340
Brother Li!

52
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:14,879
Brother Li!

53
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:21,219
Brother Li!

54
00:03:22,479 --> 00:03:22,960
Brother Li!

55
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:25,960
Once you choose this path,

56
00:03:28,599 --> 00:03:29,740
there's no turning back.

57
00:03:36,599 --> 00:03:37,340
Li Laogunzi,

58
00:03:38,159 --> 00:03:38,819
you remember this:

59
00:03:40,479 --> 00:03:41,099
The city of Songliao

60
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,759
has no place for Western Suburbs folks.

61
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,400
When you see Eastern Tyrant's men,

62
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:46,560
steer clear.

63
00:03:47,479 --> 00:03:48,439
And when you see Liu Haizhu,

64
00:03:48,719 --> 00:03:49,419
you call him your savior.

65
00:04:11,419 --> 00:04:11,740
Bro,

66
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,159
are you showing off for Haizhu today,

67
00:04:16,759 --> 00:04:17,980
or are you out for blood?

68
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,399
Drink and sing,

69
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:33,879
for life is short.

70
00:04:35,379 --> 00:04:36,500
Like the morning dew,

71
00:04:37,699 --> 00:04:39,120
so many days have passed in sorrow.

72
00:04:40,379 --> 00:04:42,600
Li Laogunzi's blade didn't cut me,

73
00:04:43,259 --> 00:04:44,699
but the look in Feng Ziwen's eyes

74
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,060
pierced straight into my soul.

75
00:04:47,839 --> 00:04:49,879
The once slender, pale scholar

76
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,899
is now the King of Hell on ice.

77
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,379
Feng Ziwen.

78
00:04:53,939 --> 00:04:54,779
The Eastern Tyrant.

79
00:04:55,379 --> 00:04:56,120
He lives

80
00:04:56,439 --> 00:04:58,000
as if only to force this world

81
00:04:58,300 --> 00:04:59,160
to pay back what it owes him,

82
00:04:59,759 --> 00:05:00,699
debt by debt,

83
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,199
until it's paid in full.

84
00:05:22,259 --> 00:05:23,980
How's Mr. Feng doing?

85
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,399
He ate a bite and fell asleep.

86
00:05:30,319 --> 00:05:31,259
But the doctor said

87
00:05:31,759 --> 00:05:32,740
he has to stay a few more days.

88
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:41,399
Thanks for all your trouble.

89
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,779
Why say that? We're family.

90
00:05:55,199 --> 00:05:56,839
I suddenly want a popsicle.

91
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:02,879
Bro.

92
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,139
I want one too.

93
00:06:04,279 --> 00:06:05,439
Why eat that stuff in the dead of winter?

94
00:06:06,319 --> 00:06:07,360
So what if I want one?

95
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:09,199
Come on.

96
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:10,300
Come with me to get popsicles.

97
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,420
No way I'm going.

98
00:06:13,519 --> 00:06:14,079
Move it.

99
00:06:26,959 --> 00:06:27,339
Zhuzi.

100
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:32,620
Are you scared today?

101
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,100
You're the one who's scared today.

102
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:49,220
Menglong was always frail growing up.

103
00:06:50,079 --> 00:06:51,519
Before passing, my parents said one thing:

104
00:06:52,959 --> 00:06:53,800
"Protect him."

105
00:06:54,939 --> 00:06:56,519
When he was six, he fell gravely ill.

106
00:06:57,459 --> 00:06:58,480
He almost didn't make it.

107
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,160
He was burning up, delirious.

108
00:07:01,019 --> 00:07:01,879
We had nothing at home.

109
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:02,600
Just the two of us.

110
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,620
Daguang and Baige,

111
00:07:05,399 --> 00:07:06,519
ran to Yellow Immortal Temple,

112
00:07:07,019 --> 00:07:08,220
kowtowing with every single step.

113
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:10,420
Two little kids.

114
00:07:10,879 --> 00:07:12,019
They said as long as Menglong recovered,

115
00:07:12,379 --> 00:07:13,360
they'd trade years off their own lives.

116
00:07:13,879 --> 00:07:15,000
They drew fortune sticks over 30 times,

117
00:07:15,459 --> 00:07:16,740
until they finally got the best blessing.

118
00:07:17,759 --> 00:07:18,839
Laughing and crying like crazy,

119
00:07:18,959 --> 00:07:20,120
they ran back and told Menglong,

120
00:07:20,759 --> 00:07:21,720
"You're gonna live to be 80!

121
00:07:22,759 --> 00:07:23,660
Destined for wealth and glory,

122
00:07:23,699 --> 00:07:25,259
a big shot, a high official!

123
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,259
You'll even care for us in our old age."

124
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,319
And your brother believed it?

125
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:30,439
He believed it.

126
00:07:31,819 --> 00:07:32,879
Believing it got him through.

127
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:34,620
Later, he kept telling me

128
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:35,920
he'd take care of me when I grow old.

129
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,620
Just a tiny kid.

130
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:41,279
You weren't that old back then either.

131
00:07:42,319 --> 00:07:43,300
They called me their brother,

132
00:07:44,759 --> 00:07:45,660
so I had to be a mountain.

133
00:07:47,259 --> 00:07:47,899
I couldn't collapse.

134
00:07:53,759 --> 00:07:55,199
You live for them,

135
00:07:56,339 --> 00:07:57,560
and they live for you.

136
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:00,360
There's more.

137
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,779
Baige was only seven back then,

138
00:08:02,939 --> 00:08:03,639
and sick herself.

139
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,259
Drawing lots over thirty times,

140
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,600
she didn't ask once for herself.

141
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,839
And Daguang, that idiot...

142
00:08:09,819 --> 00:08:10,579
without me,

143
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:12,139
he wouldn't have food or warm clothes.

144
00:08:17,019 --> 00:08:18,259
So...

145
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:19,920
you figured

146
00:08:21,839 --> 00:08:23,839
you had to trample everyone underfoot,

147
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:27,259
make everyone shudder at your name,

148
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:28,759
so that no one

149
00:08:28,839 --> 00:08:30,500
would dare lay a finger on them.

150
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,159
You never went through that.

151
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,580
You wouldn't understand.

152
00:08:41,039 --> 00:08:41,759
As for me,

153
00:08:42,019 --> 00:08:43,639
I don't get all your mind games.

154
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:45,519
I'm just a worker.

155
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:47,980
Anyway,

156
00:08:48,379 --> 00:08:50,500
every day, seeing big ships in the yard,

157
00:08:50,679 --> 00:08:51,360
I just think:

158
00:08:52,279 --> 00:08:53,360
A ship like that,

159
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:54,799
braving the winds and waves...

160
00:08:55,419 --> 00:08:56,379
no matter how huge,

161
00:08:57,039 --> 00:08:57,779
no matter how mighty,

162
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,860
there're still storms it can't beat,

163
00:09:01,539 --> 00:09:03,179
and reefs it can't survive.

164
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,639
Even a tiny spot of rust

165
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,600
could sink it.

166
00:09:10,899 --> 00:09:11,320
Zhuzi...

167
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:13,840
And you said you don't play games.

168
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:15,440
You're finding subtle ways to warn me.

169
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:17,860
I'm just talking.

170
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,960
I'm not educated like you.

171
00:09:21,059 --> 00:09:22,980
You can drop classical quotes anytime.

172
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,440
Popsicles are here!

173
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:30,500
Wait, we're really doing this?

174
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:31,399
Bring it on!

175
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,440
Let's have a contest then!

176
00:09:36,899 --> 00:09:37,360
Let's go!

177
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:39,200
Sure, why not!

178
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:41,539
I've got a special trick for this.

179
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:42,559
Three.

180
00:09:43,019 --> 00:09:43,460
Two.

181
00:09:43,799 --> 00:09:44,240
One.

182
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:45,980
Holy cow!

183
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,000
My brain is totally frozen!

184
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,539
Three total idiots.

185
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:57,559
That day in Songliao,

186
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:59,720
something even bigger happened,

187
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:01,100
something we didn't know about.

188
00:10:01,799 --> 00:10:02,480
And that event,

189
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:03,639
down the line,

190
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,899
nearly killed every single one of us.

191
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,080
Director Zhu.

192
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:13,460
Director Zhu.

193
00:10:14,259 --> 00:10:15,059
Starved out of your mind?

194
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:19,139
If I didn't bring you food today,

195
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:20,659
you wouldn't have made it, right?

196
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:24,639
Here.

197
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,139
Have a bite.

198
00:10:30,799 --> 00:10:31,480
Boss Zhang...

199
00:10:32,159 --> 00:10:33,259
Please, I beg you, let me go!

200
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:46,580
Just eat up.

201
00:10:47,379 --> 00:10:48,179
Director Zhu.

202
00:10:48,519 --> 00:10:50,120
You drank plenty of my booze,

203
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:50,879
got plenty of sleep,

204
00:10:50,899 --> 00:10:51,799
and took plenty of perks.

205
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,659
I asked you for one little favor,

206
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,139
and you acted like I wanted your life.

207
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,580
Did you think my place was a free inn?

208
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:04,419
What about our deal, then?

209
00:11:07,019 --> 00:11:08,399
We'll do the deal your way.

210
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:10,600
Director Zhu.

211
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:11,860
If you'd been this sensible earlier,

212
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,080
why suffer through all this?

213
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,000
Quick, two of you, get over here.

214
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,759
Help our Director Zhu up.

215
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,340
Untie his hands behind his back.

216
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:19,779
Easy there.

217
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,019
He's our God of Wealth.

218
00:11:21,519 --> 00:11:22,340
My good brother.

219
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:39,860
Let's get straight to the point.

220
00:11:40,639 --> 00:11:41,399
The tractor factory

221
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:43,019
lost tens of thousands of yuan worth of

222
00:11:43,179 --> 00:11:44,340
machinery, equipment, and raw materials.

223
00:11:45,659 --> 00:11:46,539
Do you know what this means?

224
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,360
This is slicing open a state artery

225
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,320
and bleeding it dry!

226
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,940
We've been ordered to solve this quickly.

227
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,779
Every precinct must screen train stations,

228
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:55,720
black markets,

229
00:11:56,559 --> 00:11:57,519
and scrap metal yards.

230
00:11:57,899 --> 00:11:58,679
Keep your eyes glued to them!

231
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,120
I'm going to make sure

232
00:12:00,179 --> 00:12:01,600
this giant rat stealing state grain

233
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:02,799
has nowhere to hide!

234
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,700
As for this case...

235
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:06,740
Comrade Kong Fanping will be in charge.

236
00:12:09,259 --> 00:12:09,919
Yes, Chief Liao!

237
00:12:10,039 --> 00:12:10,840
Alright, that's all.

238
00:12:11,059 --> 00:12:11,399
Dismissed.

239
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:20,799
Boss!

240
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,279
This is a huge case!

241
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:25,899
A big case is a good thing!

242
00:12:27,399 --> 00:12:29,220
You're a cop, and you hope for trouble?

243
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:31,940
Big cases are how you make your mark!

244
00:12:32,799 --> 00:12:33,600
Being a cop

245
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:35,740
is about preventing big cases.

246
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:37,720
Once you put on this uniform,

247
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:38,980
you have to protect the local peace.

248
00:12:39,039 --> 00:12:39,659
Got that?

249
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:40,779
Got it.

250
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:42,600
Come over here.

251
00:12:45,879 --> 00:12:46,860
Break down the case for me.

252
00:12:47,279 --> 00:12:47,639
Let's hear it.

253
00:12:48,399 --> 00:12:49,000
Boss,

254
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:51,240
the tractor factory crime scene

255
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:52,799
left no obvious traces.

256
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:55,700
It's very likely the work of veterans.

257
00:12:56,299 --> 00:12:58,879
An inside job can't be ruled out either.

258
00:13:00,639 --> 00:13:01,120
Good.

259
00:13:01,879 --> 00:13:02,740
Keep going.

260
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,200
Why did they assign it to us?

261
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,759
Because the factory is in our district?

262
00:13:08,399 --> 00:13:09,700
Yes, but not entirely.

263
00:13:10,539 --> 00:13:11,659
Our precinct has a lot of factories,

264
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,340
and complex dynamics, making it a focus.

265
00:13:14,559 --> 00:13:16,320
Our surface investigation

266
00:13:16,659 --> 00:13:17,399
must go on,

267
00:13:17,779 --> 00:13:19,440
but the murky waters beneath

268
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:20,740
need to be stirred up too.

269
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:22,740
Boss,

270
00:13:23,139 --> 00:13:24,279
do you already have an idea?

271
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:26,200
Give me a hint!

272
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:27,840
I'm not telling you.

273
00:13:28,299 --> 00:13:29,179
Why not?

274
00:13:31,659 --> 00:13:32,460
You've got a loose tongue.

275
00:13:32,779 --> 00:13:34,240
Telling you is like broadcasting it.

276
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:35,980
Boss, my lips are sealed!

277
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:37,360
Ask me any secret if you don't believe me.

278
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:38,340
I swear I won't tell.

279
00:13:41,259 --> 00:13:41,899
Last week,

280
00:13:42,919 --> 00:13:44,399
who ate the braised pork from my lunchbox?

281
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:46,320
Was it you?

282
00:13:48,659 --> 00:13:49,320
It was you.

283
00:13:50,779 --> 00:13:52,740
Boss, I was just craving it, you know?

284
00:13:53,019 --> 00:13:54,700
Besides, your wife's cooking is too good!

285
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:12,379
Brother Ma,

286
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:13,820
eat up.

287
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:30,940
Wait, what's going on here?

288
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,320
Where's Boss Zhang?

289
00:14:33,179 --> 00:14:35,799
Director Ma is a very busy man.

290
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:37,120
We're here to talk serious business.

291
00:14:37,159 --> 00:14:38,539
Why hasn't he shown up yet?

292
00:14:48,559 --> 00:14:49,620
When did Director Ma arrive?

293
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:51,039
Sorry to keep you waiting!

294
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:56,340
Zhang Haoran.

295
00:14:57,679 --> 00:14:59,019
Boss Zhang.

296
00:14:59,759 --> 00:15:01,620
I came here to talk serious business.

297
00:15:01,899 --> 00:15:03,379
Not to let you fool around like this.

298
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,320
Brother Ma.

299
00:15:06,899 --> 00:15:08,200
Put the blame on me.

300
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:09,720
I'll take a penalty drink.

301
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:10,299
No need.

302
00:15:11,899 --> 00:15:13,139
Whoever's late drinks the penalty.

303
00:15:16,019 --> 00:15:18,299
I thought you came here to see me.

304
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:20,340
Did Yan'er fail to keep you company?

305
00:15:22,279 --> 00:15:22,919
How about this...

306
00:15:24,379 --> 00:15:26,240
I'll take three penalty drinks, alright?

307
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,379
Well, look... let's do this.

308
00:15:32,419 --> 00:15:34,700
Director Ma usually drinks premium liquor.

309
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,539
This bulk liquor of yours won't do.

310
00:15:36,759 --> 00:15:37,980
It's strong. Goes straight to your head.

311
00:15:40,519 --> 00:15:41,879
Have you ever had good liquor?

312
00:15:42,179 --> 00:15:43,299
This is genuine Moutai!

313
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:45,480
Wait, what are you—

314
00:15:52,259 --> 00:15:53,740
Who gave you permission to speak here?

315
00:15:54,259 --> 00:15:54,779
Get the hell out!

316
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,100
Can't even talk like a human being!

317
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:04,220
Boss Zhang.

318
00:16:04,759 --> 00:16:05,299
That's uncalled for.

319
00:16:06,139 --> 00:16:06,899
He's your brother.

320
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,120
Well... uh...

321
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:09,399
He's done eating.

322
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:12,980
A bratty kid needs a good slap to learn.

323
00:16:14,399 --> 00:16:15,899
Sometimes when people are clueless,

324
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,980
you can't give them any face.

325
00:16:18,679 --> 00:16:19,100
Right?

326
00:16:21,539 --> 00:16:22,000
Right.

327
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,159
Director Ma.

328
00:16:33,379 --> 00:16:34,559
This jug of mine...

329
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:36,379
It might not have a label,

330
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,200
but it really is genuine Moutai.

331
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,320
It's just that with this liquor,

332
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,100
once it's all dressed up,

333
00:16:44,659 --> 00:16:45,899
it's hard to get it out.

334
00:16:46,279 --> 00:16:48,120
Some people, some things...

335
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:50,080
isn't it the exact same logic?

336
00:16:50,659 --> 00:16:51,120
Right?

337
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:03,220
Red ribbon, white porcelain bottle,

338
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:04,960
53-percent sauce-aroma liquor...

339
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:06,660
Definitely Moutai!

340
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:07,900
Moutai!

341
00:17:08,619 --> 00:17:09,579
Come on, Boss Zhang.

342
00:17:09,579 --> 00:17:10,720
Director Ma, you're quite a poet!

343
00:17:10,799 --> 00:17:11,500
Moutai, Moutai, Moutai!

344
00:17:11,579 --> 00:17:12,480
Together, together, let's drink together!

345
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:18,140
Director Ma,

346
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,180
I'll just be straightforward with you.

347
00:17:20,619 --> 00:17:22,079
We're on the same side here,

348
00:17:22,619 --> 00:17:24,099
so don't get mad at what I say.

349
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:26,039
Look at what you guys do at the plant.

350
00:17:26,859 --> 00:17:28,380
You skim off some cigarettes,

351
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,599
snag some coal...

352
00:17:30,759 --> 00:17:31,700
At most,

353
00:17:32,359 --> 00:17:33,599
aren't you just treating your boys

354
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:35,059
to a slightly better meal?

355
00:17:35,859 --> 00:17:37,819
But to be a ten-thousand-yuan household,

356
00:17:38,539 --> 00:17:39,920
you'll never manage it in this lifetime.

357
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:41,740
Well...

358
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:44,119
Boss Zhang, what do you mean by that?

359
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,740
You have... this...

360
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:51,720
a guest here today.

361
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,319
Since there's a guest here,

362
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:53,880
let's...

363
00:17:54,599 --> 00:17:55,420
not talk business.

364
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:56,779
Let's just drink and have a good time!

365
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:57,440
Wait, no.

366
00:17:57,599 --> 00:17:58,880
Me? What kind of guest am I?

367
00:17:59,059 --> 00:17:59,900
I'm not a guest!

368
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,619
I'm... I'm his own nephew.

369
00:18:01,819 --> 00:18:03,059
My uncle tells me everything.

370
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:04,240
Go ahead and talk, it's fine.

371
00:18:05,559 --> 00:18:06,559
Hey, Laifu.

372
00:18:07,099 --> 00:18:08,339
Why don't you go outside for a stroll?

373
00:18:08,799 --> 00:18:09,339
Wait, Uncle,

374
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:10,700
aren't we talking business?

375
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:11,960
Go take a walk.

376
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,279
Brother Laifu,

377
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:16,119
look at my body...

378
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,200
It keeps itching.

379
00:18:18,079 --> 00:18:19,099
Why don't you check it for me?

380
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,380
Take a look for me.

381
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:33,299
Brother Ma,

382
00:18:34,319 --> 00:18:35,180
let's keep drinking.

383
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:39,839
Boss Zhang.

384
00:18:44,599 --> 00:18:45,220
Director Ma,

385
00:18:46,779 --> 00:18:48,839
all that stuff in your factory...

386
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:50,180
Sitting in your yard,

387
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:51,740
it's basically scrap.

388
00:18:52,119 --> 00:18:53,440
But do you know that stuff,

389
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,640
once it passes Shanhai Pass,

390
00:18:56,319 --> 00:18:57,660
into the hands of certain people,

391
00:18:58,819 --> 00:19:01,400
is worth piles and piles of cash?

392
00:19:04,119 --> 00:19:06,240
You mean trafficking state assets?

393
00:19:07,539 --> 00:19:08,039
That's out of the question.

394
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,819
That's a capital offense! Who'd dare?

395
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:13,160
Lose your head? Come on.

396
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:16,000
That only happens to incompetent fools.

397
00:19:17,619 --> 00:19:18,900
With the network I, Zhang Haoran, have,

398
00:19:19,619 --> 00:19:21,440
we can do it without leaving a trace.

399
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:25,599
These goods leave your factory warehouse,

400
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,539
head to the southern ports,

401
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,819
and then go overseas.

402
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:33,700
Think of how the profit multiplies!

403
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:35,559
Director Ma,

404
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:37,420
even if you wracked your brain

405
00:19:38,059 --> 00:19:38,859
in your office all day,

406
00:19:38,859 --> 00:19:40,259
you wouldn't dare dream of such a sum.

407
00:19:40,259 --> 00:19:41,220
Just how much money is that?

408
00:19:41,579 --> 00:19:43,200
Who'd dare dream of such a thing?

409
00:19:51,019 --> 00:19:52,079
A while back,

410
00:19:52,779 --> 00:19:53,859
that business at the tractor factory...

411
00:19:54,339 --> 00:19:54,920
Was that you?
